EC2 Scenario-Based Interview Questions 🚀

Amazon EC2 is one of the most used AWS services — but real-world scenarios matter more than just definitions.

Here are 20 high-level EC2 scenario-based questions to challenge your AWS & DevOps skills 👇

1. Your EC2 instance is running but you can’t connect via SSH. What troubleshooting steps will you take?
2.	You terminated an EC2 instance by mistake. How can you prevent this in the future?
3.	Your EC2 instance needs to access an S3 bucket securely. What’s the best way to configure this?
4.	An application hosted on EC2 needs to be highly available across AZs. How will you achieve it?
5.	You need to run scheduled scripts on EC2 daily. What approaches are available?
6.	How will you enable auto-scaling for EC2 based on CPU utilization?
7.	You’re seeing high latency between EC2 and RDS in the same region. What might be wrong?
8.	You need to move an EC2 instance to another region. What are your options?
9.	Your EC2 disk space keeps filling up. How do you investigate and fix this?
10.	You have to reduce EC2 costs without affecting performance. Which AWS features can you use?
11.	An application requires high IOPS. Which EC2 storage type should you choose?
12.	You updated your security group, but traffic is still blocked. What else can you check?
13.	You need to allow only office IPs to SSH into EC2. How would you configure this?
14.	Your EC2 instance should recover automatically if the host hardware fails. What’s the best solution?
15.	How do you configure load balancing across multiple EC2 instances?
16.	How will you monitor EC2 performance metrics and set alerts?
17.	You need to share an AMI with another AWS account. How do you do it?
18.	A web app hosted on EC2 should handle traffic spikes. How do you design it?
19.	Your instance gets terminated when Spot capacity isn’t available. How can you handle this better?
20.	You need to run batch jobs once per week without leaving EC2 running all the time. What’s the best approach?
